---
// src/pages/privacy.astro — Privacy Policy. Static content page, zero JS.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Root My Android collects no email, no password, and no personal identifiers. This policy lists exactly what is stored and why."
>
  <div class="container prose" style="padding: 3rem 1.25rem">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="faint"><em>Last updated: October 20, 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      Root My Android is designed around data minimalism: accounts are random numbers, and the
      default flow collects nothing about you. This policy describes exactly what is stored, why,
      and what never is.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What we store</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account record</strong> — your randomly generated 16-digit account number, its
        creation time, credit balance, Nitro balance, and the Nitro ledger (purchases and
        consumption) attached to that number.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Device audit snapshots</strong> — only when you explicitly sync them: device
        model, Android version, and audit results (for example, which installed apps participate
        in Android backup), keyed by an app-generated device ID. Each snapshot is overwritten by
        the next sync of the same device and audit type.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Payment records</strong> — payment IDs, amounts, currencies, and transaction
        status as reported by the payment rail you used. For our self-hosted crypto processor
        (BTCPay Server), we additionally see the paying transaction ID. We never see or store
        card numbers, bank details, or your name.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Guardian pairing data</strong> — when you pair the Guardian Angel app to an
        account, the pairing record between that account number and the managed device's ID.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. What we never collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Email addresses, passwords, names, or phone numbers (there is no field to enter them).</li>
      <li>The contents of your backups — they are encrypted on your device with a key only you hold.</li>
      <li>Contacts, messages, photos, or files from your device.</li>
      <li>Advertising identifiers or cross-site tracking of any kind.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Website analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The website uses <a href="https://simpleanalytics.com" rel="noopener">Simple Analytics</a>,
      a privacy-focused service that collects no personal data, sets no cookies, and does not
      track visitors across sites. No other analytics or advertising scripts are used.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Infrastructure</h2>
    <p>
      The Service runs on Cloudflare (website, API, database, and backup storage). Cloudflare
      processes standard edge connection metadata (IP addresses, TLS parameters) to deliver and
      protect the site; our <code>/v1/device/whoami</code> endpoint echoes this metadata back to
      you on request and stores none of it. Payment processing for crypto rails is split between
      our self-hosted BTCPay Server and NOWPayments; card / Apple Pay purchases, when offered,
      are handled by a third-party on-ramp — each provider processes your payment under its own
      privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Guardian Angel application is a tool for parents and legal guardians to manage devices
      used by their minor children. It is installed and configured by the parent and syncs to the
      parent's account number. We do not knowingly collect any information directly from
      children, and no personal profile of a child is created or stored — the only records are
      the parent's account number and the managed device's audit data described above.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data sharing and disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell, rent, or share your data with anyone. Because accounts are anonymous, the
      only way data can be associated with you is through your account number or a payment trail
      on the rail you chose. We would disclose stored data only if legally compelled, and only to
      the extent it exists.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Account and ledger records are kept for the life of the account. Device audit snapshots are
      replaced on each new sync. To request deletion of data attached to an account number you
      control, contact
      <a href="mailto:support@rootmyandroid.com">support@rootmyandroid.com</a> from the device or
      payment trail that proves control of the account.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      The current version of this policy is always published at
      <a href="/privacy">rootmyandroid.com/privacy</a> with its revision date.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
